Generic single-database configuration with an async dbapi (asyncpg).

Wiring and rationale: ../DESIGN.md section 5.

Changing the schema
-------------------
After editing app/db/models.py, from the repo root:

    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"

That only WRITES a file under versions/ (no DB changes). Then:

  1. Open the generated file and read it. Autogenerate for this schema
     reliably misses:
       - the xbrl schema (first migration only: op.execute("CREATE SCHEMA ..."))
       - native enum types (taxonomy / filing_form / fiscal_period)
       - expression indexes, esp. uq_fact_natural (coalesce(period_start, period_end))
       - partial indexes (ix_fact_latest_lookup) -- usually ok, eyeball it
     Fix upgrade() and downgrade() so both are correct.

  2. Apply it:
       uv run alembic upgrade head      # run upgrade() against the DB
       uv run alembic downgrade -1      # step back one
       uv run alembic current           # what's applied now

  3. Commit the migration file together with the models.py change.

Never hand-edit a migration already applied to a shared database -- write a new one.
